                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "MinHash and similarity sketching. MinHash (Broder, 1997) provides an unbiased estimator of Jaccard similarity with variance  $ \\hat{J}(1 - \\hat{J})/m $ for  $ m $ hash functions. Locality-sensitive hashing (Leskovec et al., 2020) enables sublinear nearest-neighbor queries in Jaccard space, making per-cell audits against  $ 10^6 $-cell references computationally tractable on standard hardware.",
